  "title": "Assam's Renewable Energy Project Initiated with Adani Power",
  "summary": "Adani Power Limited's 3,200 MW thermal plant site in Assam's Dhubri has been involved in evictions following the Bodoland Territorial Council's inability to provide space in the adjoining Kokrajhar district. The project aims to secure around 5,000 jobs in Assam by December 2030.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Adani Power Limited's 3,200 MW thermal plant site in Dhubri has been involved in evictions after the Bodoland Territorial Council could not provide space in Kokrajhar.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The project is expected to generate 5,000 jobs once operational, with a phased commissioning planned from December 2030.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The plant is part of India's broader renewable energy initiatives aimed at boosting Assam's green energy capacity.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
